  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1210 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nThe overall weather pattern does not change much as we move into \nSeptember. There remains some potential that the upper ridge will \nloosen its grip slightly and shift a little further to the east. \nThis might allow for a little more potential for diurnal showers and \nstorms to affect the western Panhandles, but confidence is not high \nfor this at this moment. Overall, the bulk of the area will remain \ndry and continued above normal temperatures of upper 90s into the \n100s. Models indicate that by next weekend, the upper ridge builds \nback into the region with a big blocking pattern across the Plains \nstates with more troughing in the east and west. This is surely not \ngood news for any rainfall or hopes for a cooldown for the Labor Day \nholiday weekend.",
